            0.087,
            0.881,
            0.124
          ],
          "content": "**5. Are there cities whose population has almost doubled? Which are they?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.127,
            0.126,
            0.735,
            0.145
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:** Yes, they are Bengaluru, Hyderabad, Surat and Vadodara"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.144,
            0.155,
            0.882,
            0.193
          ],
          "content": "**6. By what number should we multiply Patna’s population to get a number/population close to that of Mumbai?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.127,
            0.195,
            0.874,
            0.233
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:** We need to multiply Patna’s population by 7.39 to get a number close to the population of Mumbai."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.248,
            0.241,
            0.266
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Page No. 14"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.277,
            0.882,
            0.336
          ],
          "content": "**Using the meaning of multiplication and division, can you explain why multiplying by 5 is the same as dividing by 2 and multiplying by 10? Ans:** $1 0 \\div 2$ is the same as 5."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.355,
            0.282,
            0.374
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "？ Figure it out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.144,
            0.386,
            0.634,
            0.405
          ],
          "content": "**1. Find quick ways to calculate these products:**"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.177,
            0.406,
            0.356,
            0.466
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{aligned}( a ) \\quad & 2 \\times 1768 \\times 50 \\\\= & 2 \\times 50 \\times 1768 \\\\= & 100 \\times 1768\\end{aligned}",
          "image_source": "images/page_31_equation_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.485,
            0.469,
            0.576
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{aligned}( b ) \\quad & 72 \\times 125 [Hint: 125 = \\frac{1000}{8}] \\\\= & 72 \\times \\frac{1000}{8} \\\\= & \\frac{72}{8} \\times 1000 = 9 \\times 1000\\end{aligned}",
          "image_source": "images/page_31_equation_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.591,
